\fs20\cgrid {\cs26\super $}{ Overview}}}{Overview
\par }\pard\plain \s27\qj\li720\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\cgrid {{\*\bkmkstart pgfId_371663}{\*\bkmkend pgfId_371663}
The COM standard allows software components written in different languages to communicate with each other. Unfortunately, building COM compliant applications requires the development of large amount of code only dedicated to support the technology. The Ei
ffelCOM wizard was designed to free programmers from writing the plumbing code. 
\par }\pard\plain \qj\fi720\li720\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\adjustright \cgrid {\f1 {\*\bkmkstart pgfId_375227}{\*\bkmkend pgfId_375227}
The EiffelCOM wizard is a powerful tool that enables the fast development of COM components in Eiffel and access COM components from Eiffel systems. It consists of a series of dialogs, which ask about the component\rquote 
s characteristics. The wizard needs the data to produce an Eiffel system skeleton, the code to access or create a component, and the component-specific runtime libraries. 
\par }\pard\plain \s29\qj\fi720\li720\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\cgrid {{\*\bkmkstart pgfId_374028}{\*\bkmkend pgfId_374028}
The wizard allows Eiffel developers with little COM knowledge to develop and reuse COM components. The design of the generated code follows the Eiffel standards and is familiar experienced Eiffel users. The only prerequisite to use the EiffelCOM wizard 
is an understanding of the }{\i Interface Definition Language}{. }{\i IDL}{ describes a component. Standard compilers can generate }{\i Type Libraries}{ from }{\i IDL}{
 files. Tools that need information on a given component, such as the EiffelCOM wizard, Visual Basic, etc. analyze Type Libraries. The }{\i IDL}{ syntax is very close to C and easy to learn. 
\par }\pard\plain \qj\fi720\li720\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\adjustright \cgrid {\f1 {\*\bkmkstart pgfId_369655}{\*\bkmkend pgfId_369655}
The wizard generates code from a Type Library and additional information given by the user. The generated code consists of Eiffel classes, C/C++ files, and library
 files. The wizard automatically produces library files from generated C and C++ code. You do not need to modify generated C/C++ code to build your EiffelCOM system. 
\par }\trowd \trgaph15\trleft660\trbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \trbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \trbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \trbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \clvertalc\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cltxlrtb \cellx6900\pard\plain 
