\par The main window includes a toolbar and a menu. The first three buttons on the toolbar correspond to the first three entries in the File menu: }{\i New}{, }{\i Open}{, and }{\i Save}{. }{\i New}{
 resets all the information previously entered in the wizard. }{\i Open}{ brings up an Open File Dialog that can be used to retrieve a previously saved EiffelCOM project. }{\i Save}{
 is used to save the current project. A project is defined by all the values entered in the wizard. It can be saved only after the wizard has been run. The file extension for an EiffelCOM project is }{\i ewz}{. 
\par }\pard\plain \qj\fi720\li720\sb100\sa100\widctlpar\adjustright \cgrid {\f1 {\*\bkmkstart pgfId_373265}{\*\bkmkend pgfId_373265}The second menu, }{\i\f1 Build}{\f1 , includes the entries }{\i\f1 Launch Wizard}{\f1  and }{\i\f1 Generate}{\f1 
 (no wizard) corresponding respectively to the last two toolbar buttons. The former activates the Generated Code Type Dialog while the
 later launches the generation with the current settings and bypasses the dialogs. This last button can be used only when a project has been loaded or when the wizard has been run once. 
\par The third menu, }{\i\f1 Help}{\f1 , includes }{\i\f1 Help}{\f1  and }{\i\f1 About EiffelCOM}{\f1 . }{\i\f1 Help}{\f1  brings up this manual. }{\i\f1 About EiffelCOM }{\f1 brings}{\i\f1  }{\f1 About EiffelCOM Dialog that gives the version number.
